course: dictionary
lesson: 15029
title: Holding back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To restrain something means to hold it back or stop it from moving. This often takes force, like a strong grip or a strap. «The seat belt restrains the child so she does not fly forward in the car.» The seat belt holds her still, so restrain must mean hold back.
explain: You can also restrain yourself. That means you stop yourself from doing something you really want to do, like shouting or laughing. «Mia had to restrain herself from laughing during the serious play.» She wanted to laugh, but she held it back.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like holding, stopping, force, and keeping still tell you that restrain means hold back. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: «The seat belt stops the child» still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: «Restrain» means to hold someone or something back, or stop them from moving or doing something.
fact: «Restrain» often needs force, such as a firm hold or a strap.
fact: «Restrain yourself» means to stop yourself from doing something you want to do, like shouting or laughing.
fact: Seat belts and car seats restrain children in cars to keep them safe.
fact: Dogs are restrained on leads so they stay safe and under control.
exercise: «Dad used the strap to restrain the box on the back seat.» What does restrain mean here? | Lift it high above the roof | Paint it bright red | Throw it out of the window | *Hold it still and stop it moving
exercise: Sam wanted to shout at the referee, but he restrained himself. What did Sam do? | Ran onto the pitch | Shouted even louder | Asked for a drink | *Stopped himself from shouting
exercise: «The dog was restrained on a lead.» Find and copy one word that is a form of restrain. | dog | lead | on | *restrained
test: «The teacher could not restrain her laughter when the class sang off key.» What does restrain mean here? | Start to sing along | Laugh even harder | *Stop herself from laughing | Forget the song
test: What is a seat belt doing when it restrains a child? | Lifting the child out of the car | *Keeping the child safely in the seat | Making the child sleepy | Warming the child up
exam: Which sentence uses restrain to mean stop yourself from doing something? | *«He restrained himself from eating the last cake.» | «The rope restrained the boat to the dock.» | «The dog restrained the ball in its mouth.» | «The wind restrained the kite in the sky.»
